From ae58146620b0478123fb2cf8c47b2432060d9a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:52:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/92] avformat/http: do not end a chunked body on the
 multi-client listener

With listen=2 the context returned by avio_open2() only accepts
connections. Closing it went through http_shutdown() like any other
HTTP context, which writes the final "0\r\n\r\n" chunk to s->hd. That
is the listening socket, so the write waits for it to become writable
and never returns, and avio_close() hangs forever.

Programs that fork a child for every client, such as the
avio_http_serve_files example, close their copy of the server in the
child. Every child stayed blocked in avio_close() instead of exiting.

Skip the chunked body terminator for the listening context. Clients
returned by avio_accept() have listen set to 0 and are not affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 libavformat/http.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
index a7854122f1..5c692369ce 100644
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -2308,7 +2308,9 @@ static int http_close(URLContext *h)
     av_freep(&s->inflate_buffer);
 #endif /* CONFIG_ZLIB */
 
-    if (s->hd && !s->end_chunked_post)
+    /* The listening context of a multi-client server has no connection of
+     * its own, and writing to a listening socket never completes. */
+    if (s->hd && !s->end_chunked_post && s->listen != HTTP_MUTLI)
         /* Close the write direction by sending the end of chunked encoding. */
         ret = http_shutdown(h, h->flags);
 
